{{Shortcut|MOS:PSEUDOHEAD|MOS:FAKEHEADING}}
{{Anchor|Pseudo-headings}}

Do not create pseudo-headings by misusing semicolon markup (<code>;</code>), which is reserved for [[Wikipedia:Manual of Style/Lists#Description (definition, association) lists|description lists]], and avoid using bold text for headings. Screen readers and other assistive technologies rely on proper heading markup for navigation. If the [[Wikipedia:Table of contents|table of contents]] (TOC) is too large, use the {{tl|TOC limit}} template to reduce the length of the TOC by hiding nested subsections, rather than a floating TOC. When {{tl|TOC limit}} cannot be used due to lower-level headings elsewhere in the article, using bold text for sub-sub-sub headings is the least disruptive alternative for screen readers. However, pseudo-headings should be used only as a last resort.

